IMPORT prelude

-- Community Titles Act 2018 (Western Australia) -- what the community corporation is and how a lot owner belongs to it
-- (ss 16(6)-(7), 17(6)-(8)), what the owner owes it and when it can charge interest (ss 85(1)-(2), 87(5)-(6), 88), how the
-- owner's vote is cast and what an ordinary or special resolution is (ss 106, 107(5)), what the scheme by-laws can and
-- cannot do to the owner (ss 43, 44, 46(5), 47, 48), the owner's own duties (ss 70-72), what the owner is told and may do
-- when buying a lot, off the plan or not (ss 97, 130-138, the s 3(1) notifiable variations), and how the owner takes a
-- dispute to the Tribunal and seeks review of its order (ss 162, 175).
--
-- SEAT: the owner of a lot in a community titles scheme (and, before settlement, the buyer who is about to become one).
-- Every decision is phrased as the owner would ask it: "How do I take part in this community corporation", "How much is
-- my contribution", "Can I cast my lot's vote", "Is this by-law invalid", "May I avoid my contract".
--
-- Provisions covered: s 3(1) (type 1 and type 2 notifiable variation, working day), s 16(6)-(7), s 17(6)-(8), s 41(1),
-- s 43(1)-(2), s 44(1)-(2), s 46(5), s 47, s 48(1), (2), (5)-(8), s 70, s 71, s 72(2), s 85(1)-(2), s 87(5)-(6),
-- s 88(1)(f)-(g), (2)-(6), s 94(2)-(4), s 97(2)-(3), s 106(3), (5)-(8), (13)(c), (14)(b), s 107(5), s 130(3)-(4),
-- s 131(3)-(4), s 132, s 133, s 134, s 135, s 136, s 137, s 138(2), s 162(1)(a), (f), (h), (3), s 175(1)-(2).
--
-- Edition: the compilation whose last amendment in operation is the Transfer of Land Amendment Act 2022 Pt 3 Div 1
-- (7 August 2023), legislation.wa.gov.au mrdoc_46400, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_46400.txt
-- (retrieved 7 September 2026); ss 224-226 and 253 uncommenced. Regulations used: Community Titles Regulations 2021,
-- version 00-r0-00, in currency from 1 July 2026, mrdoc_49620, deposited at
-- ../../../community-titles-regulations-2021/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49620.txt (retrieved 20 October 2026):
-- regs 8 (type 1 notifiable variation), 59 and Schedule 1 (breach notice explanation), 60 (by-law penalty $2 000),
-- 77 and 78 ($500 a lot or tier parcel), 79 (interest at most 11% a year), 84 (certificate fee $140, plus 10% with GST)
-- and 173 (internal review).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: planning and the community development statement's content (Part 3), scheme documents and registration
-- (Parts 4-5) except the unit entitlement's role, statutory easements, rates and taxes, the original subdivision owner's
-- own duties (Part 6) except as they reach the buyer through s 130(4), insurance (ss 73, 83-84), the community
-- corporation's property powers (ss 75-82) except s 80's recovery as a contribution (mentioned only), records and
-- registers (ss 91-96), meetings, councils and officers (ss 108-116), scheme managers (Part 9), termination (Part 11),
-- the Tribunal's orders in detail (ss 163-174), and the vote of a tier parcel (s 106(9)-(10)) except as it reaches the
-- owner. Machinery out: ss 1-2, 4-5, 177-190 and the amending Part 14.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Community Titles Act 2018 -- the lot owner's questions`

§§ `the numbers the regulations set`

-- reg 79: "For the purposes of section 88(1)(f), the maximum rate of interest payable for a contribution, or an
-- instalment of a contribution, that is in arrears is 11% per annum."
`the maximum interest rate` MEANS 11%

-- reg 77(1): the s 87(5) amount is "the number of lots and tier parcels in the community titles scheme by $500".
-- reg 78: "The amount fixed for the purposes of section 87(6)(a)(ii) is $500."
`the regulated amount per lot or tier parcel` MEANS 500

-- reg 60: "the maximum amount that may be imposed by the Tribunal by way of penalty for contravention of scheme by-laws is
-- $2 000." s 48(6)(d): "a daily penalty may be imposed for a continuing contravention only if that is authorised by the
-- regulations". No regulation in the deposited version authorises one (searched for "daily", "each day" and "per day";
-- the only hit is Schedule 1's "if the regulations authorise it").
`the regulated by-law penalty` MEANS 2000

-- reg 84(1)(c): the maximum fee "in the case of an application for a certificate under section 97 -- $140"; (3): "increased
-- by 10% if the community corporation is required to remit GST".
`the regulated certificate fee` MEANS 140

§§ `ss 16, 17 -- the community corporation and my place in it`

-- s 7(2): "A community scheme can be comprised of up to, but not more than, 3 tiers of community titles schemes." A tier 1
-- scheme divides the parcel; a tier 2 scheme divides a tier 1 lot (then called a "tier 2 parcel"); a tier 3 scheme divides
-- a tier 2 lot (ss 8-10).
DECLARE `Tier` IS ONE OF
    `tier 1`   -- my lot is in the tier 1 scheme, which divides the whole parcel
    `tier 2`   -- my lot is in a tier 2 scheme, which divides one tier 1 lot
    `tier 3`   -- my lot is in a tier 3 scheme, which divides one tier 2 lot

-- s 17(1): "On registration of a community titles scheme, a community corporation is established for the community
-- titles scheme." (3): it "is a body corporate", with perpetual succession, able to sue and be sued. (6): "A tier 1
-- corporation is comprised of ... (a) the owners, for the time being, of the tier 1 lots; (b) for each tier 2 parcel
-- belonging to the tier 1 scheme, the tier 2 corporation." (7): likewise for tier 2 and tier 3. (8): "A tier 3
-- corporation is comprised of the owners, for the time being, of the tier 3 lots". s 13(4)-(5): a tier 2 scheme belongs to
-- its tier 1 scheme; a tier 3 scheme belongs to its tier 2 scheme and to that tier 1 scheme.
DECLARE `How I take part` IS ONE OF
    `directly, as a member`                                  -- I am a member: I am levied and I vote
    `through the community corporation below it, which is the member`   -- my own corporation is the member and votes for its parcel
    `not at all`

@export How do I, as a lot owner, take part in this community corporation: as a member myself, through my own community corporation, or not at all (s 17(6)-(8))?
GIVEN `my lot's tier` IS A `Tier` @desc The tier of the community titles scheme your lot is in
      `the corporation's tier` IS A `Tier` @desc The tier of the community titles scheme whose corporation you are asking about
      `my scheme is that scheme or belongs to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your lot's scheme is that scheme, or a scheme that belongs to it (a tier 2 or tier 3 scheme carved out of it)
GIVETH A `How I take part`
DECIDE `How do I take part in this community corporation` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `my scheme is that scheme or belongs to it`)
            THEN `not at all`
        IF `my number` EQUALS `its number`
            THEN `directly, as a member`
        IF `its number` LESS THAN `my number`
            THEN `through the community corporation below it, which is the member`
        OTHERWISE `not at all`
    WHERE
        `my number` MEANS
            CONSIDER `my lot's tier`
            WHEN `tier 1` THEN 1
            WHEN `tier 2` THEN 2
            WHEN `tier 3` THEN 3
        `its number` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the corporation's tier`
            WHEN `tier 1` THEN 1
            WHEN `tier 2` THEN 2
            WHEN `tier 3` THEN 3

-- s 3(1): "relative unit entitlement of a lot or tier parcel means the proportion that the unit entitlement of the lot or
-- tier parcel bears to the sum of the unit entitlements of all the lots and tier parcels in the community titles scheme".
-- s 16(6)(b)-(d): the title carries an undivided share in the tier 1 common property (and in each higher scheme's).
-- s 16(7): "(a) a tier 1 lot owner has a share in the tier 1 common property of the same proportion as the relative unit
-- entitlement of the tier 1 lot; (b) a tier 2 lot owner has -- (i) a share in the tier 1 common property of a proportion
-- calculated by multiplying -- (I) the relative unit entitlement of the tier 2 lot; and (II) the relative unit entitlement
-- of the tier parcel of the lot's tier 2 scheme"; (c) for tier 3, the product of three relative unit entitlements.
@export What is my undivided share in the tier 1 common property of the whole community scheme (s 16(7))?
GIVEN `my lot's tier` IS A `Tier` @desc The tier of the community titles scheme your lot is in
      `my lot's unit entitlement` IS A NUMBER @desc Your lot's unit entitlement, from your scheme's schedule of unit entitlements
      `the sum in my scheme` IS A NUMBER @desc The sum of the unit entitlements of all lots and tier parcels in your scheme
      `my scheme's parcel unit entitlement` IS A NUMBER @desc For a tier 2 or tier 3 lot: the unit entitlement of your scheme's tier parcel in the scheme above it (0 for a tier 1 lot)
      `the sum in the scheme above` IS A NUMBER @desc The sum of the unit entitlements in the scheme above yours (1 for a tier 1 lot)
      `the tier 2 parcel's unit entitlement in tier 1` IS A NUMBER @desc For a tier 3 lot: the unit entitlement of the tier 2 scheme's parcel in the tier 1 scheme (0 otherwise)
      `the sum in the tier 1 scheme` IS A NUMBER @desc For a tier 3 lot: the sum of the unit entitlements in the tier 1 scheme (1 otherwise)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my share of the tier 1 common property` IS
    CONSIDER `my lot's tier`
    WHEN `tier 1` THEN `my relative unit entitlement`
    WHEN `tier 2` THEN `my relative unit entitlement` TIMES `my parcel's relative unit entitlement`
    WHEN `tier 3` THEN `my relative unit entitlement` TIMES `my parcel's relative unit entitlement`
                       TIMES (`the tier 2 parcel's unit entitlement in tier 1` DIVIDED BY `the sum in the tier 1 scheme`)
    WHERE
        `my relative unit entitlement` MEANS `my lot's unit entitlement` DIVIDED BY `the sum in my scheme`
        `my parcel's relative unit entitlement` MEANS `my scheme's parcel unit entitlement` DIVIDED BY `the sum in the scheme above`

§§ `ss 85, 87, 88 -- contributions, the funds and interest`

-- s 88(1): the community corporation "can, by ordinary resolution ... (a) fix the amount it requires by way of
-- contributions from its members". (2): "Contributions must be apportioned between the members ... according to the
-- relative unit entitlements of their lots or tier parcels, unless the scheme bylaws provide for a different method of
-- apportionment." s 45(3)(e): by-laws can provide another method "for all or specified purposes" -- the reserve fund
-- included. (3): a contribution payable by a community corporation as a member of another "must be apportioned between
-- its members" the same way -- so the same calculation passes a higher corporation's levy down to me.
@export How much must I pay as my lot's share of a contribution my community corporation has resolved to raise (s 88(2), (3))?
GIVEN `the amount resolved` IS A NUMBER @desc The total, in dollars, the community corporation resolved to raise from its members (or, under s 88(3), the amount levied on your corporation by the corporation above it)
      `my unit entitlement` IS A NUMBER @desc The unit entitlement of your lot (or of your scheme's tier parcel, when working out what the corporation above levies on your corporation)
      `the sum of the unit entitlements` IS A NUMBER @desc The sum of the unit entitlements of all lots and tier parcels in the scheme
      `the by-laws provide a different method` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the scheme by-laws provide a different method of apportionment for this contribution
      `my share under the by-law method` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, your share under it, as a fraction (for example 0.05); otherwise 0
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is my contribution` IS
    IF `the by-laws provide a different method`
    THEN `the amount resolved` TIMES `my share under the by-law method`
    ELSE `the amount resolved` TIMES `my unit entitlement` DIVIDED BY `the sum of the unit entitlements`

-- s 88(3) applied at both levels, apportioning by relative unit entitlement at each (the encoder assumes neither scheme's
-- by-laws provide a different method; where one does, use `How much is my contribution` twice with the by-law shares).
@export How much of a levy raised by the tier 1 community corporation reaches me, a tier 2 lot owner, through my own corporation (s 88(2), (3))?
GIVEN `the tier 1 levy` IS A NUMBER @desc The total, in dollars, the tier 1 corporation resolved to raise from its members
      `my tier 2 parcel's unit entitlement` IS A NUMBER @desc The unit entitlement of your tier 2 scheme's parcel in the tier 1 schedule
      `the sum in the tier 1 scheme` IS A NUMBER @desc The sum of the unit entitlements in the tier 1 scheme
      `my lot's unit entitlement` IS A NUMBER @desc Your lot's unit entitlement in the tier 2 schedule
      `the sum in my tier 2 scheme` IS A NUMBER @desc The sum of the unit entitlements in your tier 2 scheme
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of the tier 1 levy reaches me` IS
    `How much is my contribution`
        (`How much is my contribution` `the tier 1 levy` `my tier 2 parcel's unit entitlement` `the sum in the tier 1 scheme` FALSE 0)
        `my lot's unit entitlement` `the sum in my tier 2 scheme` FALSE 0

-- s 85(1): "A community corporation must establish -- (a) ... an administrative fund ...; and (b) ... a reserve fund". (2):
-- it "must ensure ... that there is a 10 year plan for the reserve fund", revised "at least once in each 5 years". Unlike
-- the Strata Titles Act 1985 s 100(2), (7), this is not limited to a "designated" corporation: every community corporation.
@export Must my community corporation keep a reserve fund and a 10 year plan, so that I will be levied for it (s 85(1), (2))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my community corporation keep a reserve fund` IF TRUE

-- s 88(4): a contribution "is payable on the date specified for payment in a notice served by the community corporation
-- on the member". (5): "The notice must -- (a) specify -- (i) the amount ...; (ii) the date for payment; (iii) if a
-- contribution, instalment or interest is in arrears, the amount outstanding; (iv) the amount that will become payable if
-- the contribution or instalment is not paid on or before the due date or the rate of interest payable on any amount in
-- arrears; and (v) the apportionment ... between the administrative fund and the reserve fund; and (b) be served at least
-- 14 days before the date for payment."
@export Is the contribution notice my community corporation served on me a valid one, so that the contribution falls due on its date (s 88(4), (5))?
GIVEN `it states the amount, the due date and the split between the funds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice states the amount, the date for payment and how it is split between the administrative and reserve funds
      `it states any arrears and what paying late will cost` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it states any amount already outstanding and the amount or interest rate that applies if you pay late
      `days between service and the due date` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days before the date for payment the notice was served on you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my contribution notice valid` IF
        `it states the amount, the due date and the split between the funds`
    AND `it states any arrears and what paying late will cost`
    AND `days between service and the due date` AT LEAST 14

-- s 88(1): the corporation can by ordinary resolution "(e) inflate the contribution or instalment payable to allow for a
-- discount if a contribution or instalment is paid on or before the due date ...; and (f) if the contribution or
-- instalment is not inflated and discounted, fix a rate of interest payable for a contribution, or an instalment ..., that
-- is in arrears (subject to any limitations imposed by the regulations); and (g) determine not to charge interest or to
-- charge a lesser rate of interest in a particular case or in a class of cases". reg 79: at most 11% a year.
-- Unlike the Strata Titles Act 1985 s 100(4)(b), the Act sets no default rate: the encoder reads it that no interest runs
-- unless the corporation has fixed a rate (an inference from (f)); a rate fixed above 11% is read down to 11% (an
-- inference). The rate is a year's rate, counted by days over a 365-day year (an inference: the text does not say how a
-- part-year is counted).
@export How much interest can my community corporation charge me on a contribution I paid late (s 88(1)(e)-(g); reg 79)?
GIVEN `the amount unpaid` IS A NUMBER @desc The contribution or instalment, in dollars, left unpaid after it fell due
      `the days it was overdue` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days from the due date until it was paid
      `the contribution was inflated for an early-payment discount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the corporation used the inflate-and-discount method for this contribution instead of interest
      `my corporation fixed an arrears interest rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the corporation has fixed, by ordinary resolution, a rate of interest on arrears
      `the rate it fixed` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, that yearly rate as a fraction (for example 0.1 for 10%); otherwise 0
      `it set a lesser rate or none for my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the corporation decided not to charge interest, or to charge less, in your case or a class of cases including yours
      `that lesser rate` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, that yearly rate as a fraction (0 for no interest); otherwise 0
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much interest do I owe` IS
    `the amount unpaid` TIMES `the rate that applies` TIMES `the days it was overdue` DIVIDED BY 365
    WHERE
        `the capped rate` MEANS
            IF `the rate it fixed` GREATER THAN `the maximum interest rate` THEN `the maximum interest rate` ELSE `the rate it fixed`
        `the rate that applies` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the contribution was inflated for an early-payment discount` THEN 0
                IF (NOT `my corporation fixed an arrears interest rate`) THEN 0
                IF `it set a lesser rate or none for my case` AND `that lesser rate` LESS THAN `the capped rate` THEN `that lesser rate`
                OTHERWISE `the capped rate`

-- s 88(6): "Payment of a contribution, instalment or interest is enforceable jointly and severally against the members of
-- a community corporation and the subsequent members of the community corporation." s 97(2): within 14 days of an
-- application the corporation must certify, for a lot, the contributions determined, "any amount owed ... that is
-- outstanding" and "the rate of interest payable"; (3): the certificate "is conclusive evidence of the matters stated in
-- the certificate, as at the date of the certificate, in favour of a person taking an estate or interest in a lot for
-- valuable consideration". The encoder's reading of the two together (as for the Strata Titles Act baseline): what the
-- certificate stated as owing at its date caps what the buyer can be made to pay for that period; later arrears are not
-- covered by it.
@export Having bought my lot, how much of the previous owner's unpaid contributions and interest can the community corporation make me pay (s 88(6), s 97(3))?
GIVEN `the arrears at the certificate date` IS A NUMBER @desc Contributions and interest, in dollars, actually unpaid at the date of the s 97 certificate (or at settlement, if you had no certificate)
      `the arrears arising after the certificate date` IS A NUMBER @desc Contributions and interest, in dollars, that fell unpaid after the certificate date and before you became owner (0 if no certificate)
      `I bought with a s 97 certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (or your settlement agent) obtained a certificate under s 97(2) for the lot before buying it
      `the arrears the certificate stated` IS A NUMBER @desc The outstanding amount the certificate stated, in dollars (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of the previous owner's arrears must I pay` IS
    IF `I bought with a s 97 certificate`
    THEN `the lesser of` `the arrears at the certificate date` `the arrears the certificate stated` PLUS `the arrears arising after the certificate date`
    ELSE `the arrears at the certificate date` PLUS `the arrears arising after the certificate date`
    WHERE
        GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
        `the lesser of` a b MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

-- s 87(5): a budget or variation providing for expenditure on common property under s 75(2)(b) "(other than expenditure on
-- sustainability infrastructure) exceeding an amount determined under the regulations ... must be approved by special
-- resolution". reg 77(1): lots and tier parcels times $500.
@export Must a budget that spends on improving or altering the common property be approved by special resolution, so that my vote counts against it (s 87(5); reg 77)?
GIVEN `the improvement spending` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars the budget or variation provides for improving or altering the common property (not sustainability infrastructure)
      `the number of lots and tier parcels` IS A NUMBER @desc How many lots and tier parcels there are in the community titles scheme
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the improvement budget pass by special resolution` IF
    `the improvement spending` GREATER THAN `the number of lots and tier parcels` TIMES `the regulated amount per lot or tier parcel`

-- s 87(6): "A community corporation must not make any expenditure that is not authorised by an approved budget except for --
-- (a) expenditure of an amount not exceeding, in a financial year, for each lot or tier parcel ... (i) the amount fixed by
-- the community corporation by special resolution; or (ii) if [none], the amount fixed by the regulations [$500, reg 78];
-- or (b) expenditure required by a court or tribunal or by a notice or order given under a written law". Unlike the
-- Strata Titles Act 1985 s 102(6)(b), there is no notice-and-objection route.
@export Can my community corporation spend money that the approved budget does not authorise, without a further vote (s 87(6); reg 78)?
GIVEN `the unbudgeted spending this financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc Total dollars spent this financial year outside the approved budget, including the proposed item
      `the number of lots and tier parcels` IS A NUMBER @desc How many lots and tier parcels there are in the community titles scheme
      `a per-lot amount was fixed by special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the corporation has fixed its own amount per lot or tier parcel by special resolution
      `the per-lot amount fixed` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, that amount in dollars; otherwise 0
      `a court, tribunal or written-law notice requires it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court, the Tribunal or a notice or order under a written law requires the spending
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the community corporation spend outside the budget` IF
        `the unbudgeted spending this financial year` AT MOST `the number of lots and tier parcels` TIMES `the per-lot amount`
    OR  `a court, tribunal or written-law notice requires it`
    WHERE
        `the per-lot amount` MEANS
            IF `a per-lot amount was fixed by special resolution`
            THEN `the per-lot amount fixed`
            ELSE `the regulated amount per lot or tier parcel`

§§ `ss 106, 107 -- my lot's vote`

DECLARE `Kind of resolution` IS ONE OF
    `an ordinary resolution`   -- s 106(6): more value for than against
    `a special resolution`     -- s 106(7): more than 3/4 (or 2/3) of all the unit entitlements in favour

-- s 106(5): "(a) 1 vote may be cast for each lot and each tier parcel ...; (b) the value of the vote is the unit entitlement
-- of the lot or tier parcel." (6): an ordinary resolution passes "if the value of the votes cast in favour ... is more than
-- the value of the votes cast against".
@export Did the resolution pass as an ordinary resolution of my community corporation (s 106(5), (6))?
GIVEN `the unit entitlement voting for` IS A NUMBER @desc The total unit entitlement of the lots and tier parcels whose votes were cast in favour
      `the unit entitlement voting against` IS A NUMBER @desc The total unit entitlement of those whose votes were cast against
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did it pass as an ordinary resolution` IF
    `the unit entitlement voting for` GREATER THAN `the unit entitlement voting against`

-- s 106(3): a resolution can only be put if written notice, with its terms and the voting system, "is given to all members
-- ... at least 14 days before the vote". (7): a special resolution passes if "(a) the value of the votes cast in favour ...
-- total more than 3/4 of the sum of the unit entitlements of all the lots and tier parcels in the community titles scheme;
-- or (b) for a community corporation with only 2 or 3 members, ... more than 2/3 of the sum". The measure is all the unit
-- entitlements in the scheme, not those voting, and there is no limb on votes against.
@export Did the resolution pass as a special resolution, the kind needed to make a by-law that binds me (s 106(3), (7))?
GIVEN `14 days' notice of its terms was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every member got written notice of the terms and voting system at least 14 days before the vote
      `the number of members` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members the community corporation has (lot owners and member corporations)
      `the sum of the unit entitlements` IS A NUMBER @desc The sum of the unit entitlements of all lots and tier parcels in the scheme
      `the unit entitlement voting for` IS A NUMBER @desc The total unit entitlement of those whose votes were cast in favour
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did it pass as a special resolution` IF
    `14 days' notice of its terms was given` AND `the unit entitlement voting for` GREATER THAN `the sum of the unit entitlements` TIMES `the fraction`
    WHERE
        `the fraction` MEANS
            IF `the number of members` AT MOST 3 THEN 2 DIVIDED BY 3 ELSE 3 DIVIDED BY 4

-- s 106(13): by-laws "(c) can exclude a member ... whose contributions to the community corporation are overdue from voting
-- on a resolution that may be passed as an ordinary resolution". (14)(b): they "cannot exclude a member ... from voting on a
-- resolution that is required to be a special resolution". Unlike the Strata Titles Act 1985 s 120(2), the Act itself
-- takes no vote away: only a by-law can, and only for ordinary resolutions.
@export Can I cast my lot's vote on this resolution even though my contributions are overdue (s 106(13)(c), (14)(b))?
GIVEN `the resolution` IS A `Kind of resolution` @desc The kind of resolution being voted on
      `my contributions are overdue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any contribution of yours to the community corporation is overdue
      `the by-laws exclude members in arrears` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the scheme by-laws exclude members with overdue contributions from voting on ordinary resolutions
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I cast my lot's vote` IF
        (NOT `my contributions are overdue`)
    OR  (NOT `the by-laws exclude members in arrears`)
    OR  `the resolution` EQUALS `a special resolution`

-- s 106(8): "The vote attached to a lot -- (a) is exercisable by the owner of the lot; and (b) if 2 or more persons own the
-- lot, is exercisable only through the owners jointly appointing a proxy." s 107(1): a member can appoint a proxy in
-- writing; (5): "If a member ... who is an individual and who is the sole owner of a lot is present at a meeting ..., the
-- member must cast the member's vote personally rather than by proxy." The Act gives a mortgagee no vote (contrast Strata
-- Titles Act 1985 s 126(a)).
DECLARE `Who casts my lot's vote` IS ONE OF
    `nobody, while my contributions are overdue`
    `my co-owners and I, only through one proxy we appoint jointly`
    `I must, in person, because I am at the meeting`
    `I do, in person or by proxy`

@export Who may cast my lot's vote on a resolution of the community corporation (ss 106(8), (13)(c), 107(5))?
GIVEN `the resolution` IS A `Kind of resolution` @desc The kind of resolution being voted on
      `my contributions are overdue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any contribution of yours to the community corporation is overdue
      `the by-laws exclude members in arrears` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the scheme by-laws exclude members with overdue contributions from voting on ordinary resolutions
      `I own the lot with co-owners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you own the lot together with someone else
      `I am present at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are present at the meeting where the vote is taken
GIVETH A `Who casts my lot's vote`
DECIDE `Who may cast my lot's vote` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `Can I cast my lot's vote` `the resolution` `my contributions are overdue` `the by-laws exclude members in arrears`)
            THEN `nobody, while my contributions are overdue`
        IF `I own the lot with co-owners`
            THEN `my co-owners and I, only through one proxy we appoint jointly`
        IF `I am present at the meeting`
            THEN `I must, in person, because I am at the meeting`
        OTHERWISE `I do, in person or by proxy`

§§ `ss 43-48 -- what the by-laws can and cannot do to me`

-- s 47: "Scheme bylaws are invalid as follows -- (a) to the extent that there is no power to make the bylaws; (b) ...
-- inconsistent with this Act or any other written law; (c) ... inconsistent with the community development statement ...;
-- (d) ... a restricted use condition; (e) for bylaws for a tier 2 scheme, ... inconsistent with bylaws for the tier 1
-- scheme ...; (f) for bylaws for a tier 3 scheme, ... inconsistent with bylaws for a related community titles scheme;
-- (g) ... deny or limit the right of a member ... to vote ... other than by preventing the member from voting on a
-- resolution that is not required to be a special resolution if there are outstanding contributions ...; (h) ... prohibit
-- or restrict the devolution of a lot or a transfer, lease, mortgage or other dealing with a lot; (i) ... discharge or
-- modify an easement or restrictive covenant; (j) ... the keeping on a lot of an animal that is used as an assistance
-- animal by a person with a disability ...; (k) ... the use on the tier parcel of an assistance animal ...; (l) ... (i)
-- unfairly prejudicial to, or unfairly discriminatory against, 1 or more of the owners of lots; or (ii) ... oppressive or
-- unreasonable."
DECLARE `What the by-law does` HAS
    `is beyond any power to make it`                                   IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 47(a)
    `is inconsistent with the Act or another written law`              IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 47(b)
    `is inconsistent with the community development statement`        IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 47(c)
    `is inconsistent with a restricted use condition`                  IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 47(d)
    `is inconsistent with the by-laws of a higher-tier scheme`         IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 47(e), (f)
    `limits a member's vote beyond barring arrears on ordinary resolutions` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 47(g)
    `restricts selling, leasing, mortgaging or passing on a lot`       IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 47(h)
    `discharges or modifies an easement or restrictive covenant`       IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 47(i)
    `restricts an assistance animal of a person with a disability`     IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 47(j), (k)
    `is unfairly prejudicial, discriminatory, oppressive or unreasonable, as the Tribunal finds` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 47(l): a judgment for the Tribunal

@export Is this by-law of my community titles scheme invalid against me (s 47)?
GIVEN `the by-law` IS A `What the by-law does` @desc What the by-law does, as a set of yes/no facts (the last one is the Tribunal's judgment)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this by-law invalid` IF
        `the by-law`'s `is beyond any power to make it`
    OR  `the by-law`'s `is inconsistent with the Act or another written law`
    OR  `the by-law`'s `is inconsistent with the community development statement`
    OR  `the by-law`'s `is inconsistent with a restricted use condition`
    OR  `the by-law`'s `is inconsistent with the by-laws of a higher-tier scheme`
    OR  `the by-law`'s `limits a member's vote beyond barring arrears on ordinary resolutions`
    OR  `the by-law`'s `restricts selling, leasing, mortgaging or passing on a lot`
    OR  `the by-law`'s `discharges or modifies an easement or restrictive covenant`
    OR  `the by-law`'s `restricts an assistance animal of a person with a disability`
    OR  `the by-law`'s `is unfairly prejudicial, discriminatory, oppressive or unreasonable, as the Tribunal finds`

-- s 43(1): by-laws registered with the scheme "will be taken to have been made by the community corporation"; (2): it "may
-- make further scheme bylaws by special resolution" -- one kind of resolution for every by-law (contrast the Strata Titles
-- Act 1985 s 44(2), governance and conduct). s 44(1)(b), (2): they apply to "a member, for the time being", who "must
-- comply with the bylaws as if the bylaws were a deed ... containing mutual covenants". s 46(5): exclusive use by-laws "can
-- only be made or amended if the owner of each lot that is or is proposed to be a special lot ... has given written
-- consent".
@export Does this by-law bind me as an owner: was it made the way the Act requires, and is it valid (ss 43(1)-(2), 44(2), 46(5), 47)?
GIVEN `it was registered with the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the by-law was among the scheme by-laws registered when the scheme was registered
      `it passed as a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the resolution that made it passed as a special resolution
      `it is an exclusive use by-law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it gives the occupiers of particular lots exclusive use of, or special privileges over, common property
      `every special lot owner consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether the owner of each such lot gave written consent
      `the by-law` IS A `What the by-law does` @desc What the by-law does, as a set of yes/no facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this by-law bind me` IF
        (`it was registered with the scheme` OR `it passed as a special resolution`)
    AND ((NOT `it is an exclusive use by-law`) OR `every special lot owner consented in writing`)
    AND (NOT `Is this by-law invalid` `the by-law`)

-- s 48(2): the corporation's written notice to a person alleged to have contravened the by-laws "must -- (a) specify the
-- particular scheme bylaw ...; (b) specify the particular facts relied on ...; (c) specify the action that must be taken or
-- refrained from ...; and (d) contain an explanation of the effect of this section in terms set out in the regulations"
-- (reg 59: Schedule 1 to the regulations).
@export Is the by-law breach notice my community corporation gave me a valid notice (s 48(2); reg 59)?
GIVEN `it names the by-law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice specifies the particular by-law said to be broken
      `it states the facts relied on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it specifies the facts relied on as evidence
      `it states what I must do or stop doing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it specifies what you must do or refrain from doing
      `it carries the regulations' explanation of s 48` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it includes the explanation of s 48 in the form of Schedule 1 to the regulations
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the breach notice valid` IF
    `it names the by-law` AND `it states the facts relied on` AND `it states what I must do or stop doing` AND `it carries the regulations' explanation of s 48`

-- s 48(1)(b): the corporation may apply to the Tribunal for an order enforcing the by-laws if "(i) the contravention has had
-- serious adverse consequences for a person other than the person alleged to have contravened ...; or (ii) the person has
-- contravened the particular scheme bylaw on at least 3 separate occasions; or (iii) the person has been given notice under
-- paragraph (a) and has contravened the notice". (3), (4): a member, mortgagee or occupier may apply on the same grounds.
@export Can the community corporation (or another owner or occupier) take me to the Tribunal to enforce a by-law against me (s 48(1)(b), (3), (4))?
GIVEN `it seriously harmed someone else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the breach had serious adverse consequences for someone other than you
      `the times I have broken that by-law` IS A NUMBER @desc On how many separate occasions you have broken that particular by-law
      `I broke a valid breach notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were given a written breach notice under s 48(1)(a) and then contravened it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be taken to the Tribunal over a by-law` IF
        `it seriously harmed someone else`
    OR  `the times I have broken that by-law` AT LEAST 3
    OR  `I broke a valid breach notice`

-- s 48(5)(a): the Tribunal may order the person to "pay a specified amount to the community corporation by way of penalty";
-- (6)(c) "the penalty must not exceed an amount fixed by the regulations" ($2 000, reg 60). (8): an amount a member is
-- ordered to pay is recovered, with interest, "as if the amount payable were an unpaid contribution".
@export What is the most the Tribunal can order me to pay as a penalty for breaking a by-law (s 48(6)(c); reg 60), in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be made to pay for a by-law breach` IS `the regulated by-law penalty`

@export Can the Tribunal impose a daily penalty on me for a continuing by-law breach (s 48(6)(d))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be given a daily penalty for a by-law breach` IF FALSE

§§ `ss 70-72 -- my own duties as owner`

-- s 70: "An owner or occupier of a lot ... commits an offence if the owner or occupier uses, or permits to be used, an area
-- or space in a manner that contravenes a restricted use condition set out in the scheme plan". "Penalty: (a) a fine of
-- $10 000; (b) a daily penalty of a fine of $1 000 for each day or part of a day during which the offence continues."
@export What is the most I can be fined for using part of the scheme against a restricted use condition on the scheme plan (s 70), in dollars?
GIVEN `the days or part days it continued` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days or part days the offence continued (0 for a single occasion)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for breaching a restricted use condition` IS
    10000 PLUS 1000 TIMES `the days or part days it continued`

-- s 71: "The owner or occupier of a lot must not use, or permit the use of, the lot, or common property ..., in a way that
-- interferes unreasonably with the use or enjoyment of another lot or the common property by a person who is lawfully on
-- the lot or common property." Whether it is unreasonable is for the Tribunal, so it is an input.
@export Am I in breach of my duty not to interfere unreasonably with others' use and enjoyment (s 71)?
GIVEN `my use interferes with another lot or the common property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the way you use (or let others use) the lot or common property interferes with someone lawfully on another lot or the common property
      `the Tribunal would find it unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the interference is unreasonable, as the Tribunal would find
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I breaching the use and enjoyment duty` IF
    `my use interferes with another lot or the common property` AND `the Tribunal would find it unreasonable`

-- s 72(2): "If the owner of a lot is ordinarily resident overseas or is a body corporate that is not registered in
-- Australia -- (a) the owner must nominate in writing to the community corporation a person who is ordinarily resident in
-- Australia or a body corporate registered in Australia to be the owner's agent".
@export Must I nominate an agent in Australia to the community corporation (s 72(2))?
GIVEN `I am ordinarily resident overseas` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you ordinarily live outside Australia
      `I am a body corporate not registered in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the owner is a company not registered in Australia
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I nominate an agent in Australia` IF
    `I am ordinarily resident overseas` OR `I am a body corporate not registered in Australia`

§§ `ss 94, 97 -- the certificate of what is owing`

-- s 94(2): a person with a proper interest includes "(a) a member of the community corporation" and "(c) a buyer who has
-- entered into a contract for the sale and purchase of a lot". (3), (4): the corporation may charge a fee not exceeding the
-- regulations' amount. s 97(2): within 14 days, the certificate of contributions and amounts outstanding for the lot;
-- penalty for not giving it "a fine of $3 000".
@export What is the most my community corporation may charge me for a s 97 certificate (s 94(4); reg 84), in dollars?
GIVEN `the corporation must remit GST for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the community corporation is required to remit GST on the fee
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be charged for a certificate` IS
    IF `the corporation must remit GST for it`
    THEN `the regulated certificate fee` TIMES 110%
    ELSE `the regulated certificate fee`

DECLARE `Party to my application` IS ONE OF `the community corporation`
DECLARE `Step owed to me` IS ONE OF `give me the s 97 certificate`

-- @export What is the community corporation's duty to give me the s 97 certificate I applied for, and by when (s 97(2))?
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party to my application` `Step owed to me`
DECIDE `the community corporation's duty to give me the certificate` IS
    PARTY  `the community corporation`
    MUST   `give me the s 97 certificate`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the community corporation`

@export Within how many days must the community corporation give me the s 97 certificate after my application is duly made (s 97(2); reg 84(2))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Within how many days must I get the certificate` IS 14

§§ `ss 3, 130-138 -- buying a lot`

-- s 130(3), (4): where "(a) the community titles scheme has not been registered; or (b) the first annual general meeting
-- of the community corporation has not been held; or (c) the original subdivision owner owns lots ... with an aggregate
-- relative unit entitlement of 50% or more; or (d) if the relative unit entitlement of a tier parcel in the community titles
-- scheme is 50% or more, and the original subdivision owner owns lots in the community titles scheme of that tier parcel
-- with an aggregate relative unit entitlement of 50% or more; or (e) the original subdivision owner otherwise controls 50%
-- or more of the voting power", and the original subdivision owner is the seller, the seller must also give the buyer the
-- estimated income and expenditure for 12 months after settlement, the s 67 disclosures and the services contracts.
@export As a buyer from the original subdivision owner, must I also be given the corporation's estimated budget and the owner's contracts and disclosures before I sign (s 130(3), (4))?
GIVEN `the seller is the original subdivision owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are buying from the developer who created the lot by the subdivision
      `the scheme is registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the community titles scheme has been registered
      `the first annual general meeting has been held` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the community corporation's first annual general meeting has been held
      `the seller's relative unit entitlement` IS A NUMBER @desc The fraction of the scheme's total unit entitlement carried by the lots the seller owns (for example 0.6)
      `a tier parcel carries half or more of the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a tier parcel in the scheme has a relative unit entitlement of 50% or more
      `the seller's share of that parcel's scheme` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, the fraction of the unit entitlement in that tier parcel's scheme carried by the seller's lots; otherwise 0
      `the seller otherwise controls half the voting power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller otherwise controls 50% or more of the voting power of the members
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the seller give me its extra disclosures` IF
        `the seller is the original subdivision owner`
    AND (    (NOT `the scheme is registered`)
          OR (NOT `the first annual general meeting has been held`)
          OR `the seller's relative unit entitlement` AT LEAST 50%
          OR (`a tier parcel carries half or more of the scheme` AND `the seller's share of that parcel's scheme` AT LEAST 50%)
          OR `the seller otherwise controls half the voting power`)

-- s 3(1): "type 1 notifiable variation means any of the following that occur after a contract ... but before the settlement
-- date -- (a) the area or size of the lot or proposed lot is reduced by 5% or more ...; (b) the relative unit entitlement,
-- or a reasonable estimate of [it], of the lot is increased by 5% or more, or decreased by 5% or more, from the relative unit
-- entitlement ... notified to the buyer ...; (c) anything relating to a proposal for the termination of the community titles
-- scheme is served on the seller by the community corporation; (d) any other event classified by the regulations". reg 8:
-- termination papers for a community titles scheme "other than the community titles scheme to which the seller's lot
-- belongs" served on the seller are also type 1. "type 2 notifiable variation" -- those "that do not give rise to a type 1":
-- the community development statement modified; the scheme plan modified so as to affect the lot or common property; the
-- schedule of unit entitlements modified so as to affect the lot; the by-laws modified; a services contract entered or
-- varied; a lease, licence, right or privilege over common property granted or varied. The encoder reads "increased by 5%"
-- as a change of 5% of the notified proportion, not 5 percentage points (as for the Strata Titles Act baseline).
DECLARE `Notifiable variation` IS ONE OF
    `a type 1 notifiable variation`
    `a type 2 notifiable variation`
    `no notifiable variation`

DECLARE `What changed before settlement` HAS
    `the notified area of the lot`                     IS A NUMBER    -- square metres told to the buyer before signing
    `the area of the lot now`                          IS A NUMBER
    `the notified unit entitlement`                    IS A NUMBER    -- of the lot, or its reasonable estimate (s 130(2)(b))
    `the notified sum of unit entitlements`            IS A NUMBER
    `the unit entitlement now`                         IS A NUMBER
    `the sum of unit entitlements now`                 IS A NUMBER
    `termination papers were served on the seller`     IS A BOOLEAN   -- for this or any other scheme in the community scheme (s 3(1)(c); reg 8)
    `the community development statement was modified` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the scheme plan was modified affecting the lot or common property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the by-laws were modified`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `a services contract was entered or varied`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `a lease or licence over common property was granted or varied` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Did what changed between my signing and settlement amount to a type 1 or type 2 notifiable variation (s 3(1); reg 8)?
GIVEN `the change` IS A `What changed before settlement` @desc What changed after you signed the contract and before settlement
GIVETH A `Notifiable variation`
DECIDE `What kind of notifiable variation is it` IS
    BRANCH
        IF     `the area fell by 5% or more`
            OR `the relative unit entitlement moved by 5% or more`
            OR `the change`'s `termination papers were served on the seller`
            THEN `a type 1 notifiable variation`
        IF     `the change`'s `the community development statement was modified`
            OR `the change`'s `the scheme plan was modified affecting the lot or common property`
            OR `the unit entitlement schedule changed for the lot`
            OR `the change`'s `the by-laws were modified`
            OR `the change`'s `a services contract was entered or varied`
            OR `the change`'s `a lease or licence over common property was granted or varied`
            THEN `a type 2 notifiable variation`
        OTHERWISE `no notifiable variation`
    WHERE
        `the area fell by 5% or more` MEANS
            `the change`'s `the area of the lot now` AT MOST `the change`'s `the notified area of the lot` TIMES 95%
        `the notified proportion` MEANS
            `the change`'s `the notified unit entitlement` DIVIDED BY `the change`'s `the notified sum of unit entitlements`
        `the proportion now` MEANS
            `the change`'s `the unit entitlement now` DIVIDED BY `the change`'s `the sum of unit entitlements now`
        `the relative unit entitlement moved by 5% or more` MEANS
                `the proportion now` AT LEAST `the notified proportion` TIMES 105%
            OR  `the proportion now` AT MOST `the notified proportion` TIMES 95%
        `the unit entitlement schedule changed for the lot` MEANS
                (NOT (`the change`'s `the unit entitlement now` EQUALS `the change`'s `the notified unit entitlement`))
            OR  (NOT (`the change`'s `the sum of unit entitlements now` EQUALS `the change`'s `the notified sum of unit entitlements`))

-- s 132(1): "A buyer may, by written notice to the seller, postpone the settlement date ... if the seller has not complied
-- with section 130 or 131." (2): "by no more than 15 working days after the latest date on which the seller complies".
@export As a buyer, may I postpone settlement because the seller has not given me the required information (s 132)?
GIVEN `the seller complied with s 130` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller gave you everything s 130 requires before you signed
      `the seller complied with s 131` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller notified every notifiable variation as s 131 requires (true if none occurred)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I postpone settlement` IF
    (NOT `the seller complied with s 130`) OR (NOT `the seller complied with s 131`)

-- s 133(1): the buyer may avoid before settlement "(a) if the seller has not complied with section 130; and (b) if the
-- seller were now to comply ..., the buyer would receive information or a document that would disclose material prejudice
-- to the buyer (proof of which lies on the buyer)". (2): after a substantially complying notice, "only if the buyer does so
-- within 15 working days after the seller's notice".
@export As a buyer, may I avoid my contract because the seller did not give me the s 130 information before I signed (s 133)?
GIVEN `the seller complied with s 130` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller gave you everything s 130 requires before you signed
      `the missing information shows material prejudice to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the information not given would disclose material prejudice to you (you must prove it)
      `settlement has happened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract has already settled
      `the seller has since given substantially complying notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller has since given a notice substantially complying with s 130
      `working days since that notice` IS A NUMBER @desc Working days since that late notice was given (0 if none)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I avoid for missing disclosure` IF
        (NOT `settlement has happened`)
    AND (NOT `the seller complied with s 130`)
    AND `the missing information shows material prejudice to me`
    AND (    (NOT `the seller has since given substantially complying notice`)
          OR `working days since that notice` AT MOST 15)

-- s 131(3): notice of a notifiable variation is due "(a) if the seller becomes aware ... less than 15 working days before
-- the settlement date -- as soon as practicable; and (b) in any other case -- not later than 10 working days after the seller
-- becomes aware". (4): no notice is needed where the contract described the proposed change and it matched when completed.
-- s 134: avoidance "within 15 working days after the seller gives the buyer a notice under section 131(1)" if s 131(4) does
-- not apply and "the buyer is materially prejudiced". s 135: for a type 1 variation the seller did not "substantially
-- comply" in time with, the buyer may avoid before settlement, and after a late notice within 15 working days of it. s 136:
-- the same for type 2, but only where the information "would disclose material prejudice to the buyer".
@export As a buyer, may I avoid my contract because of a notifiable variation between signing and settlement (ss 131, 134-136)?
GIVEN `the variation` IS A `Notifiable variation` @desc The kind of notifiable variation that occurred
      `the contract foretold it and it matched` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract described the proposed change and the change as completed matched (s 131(4))
      `the seller notified it in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller gave you notice of it within the time s 131(3) allows
      `the seller has given notice of it at all` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller has given you notice of the variation at any time
      `working days since the notice` IS A NUMBER @desc Working days since that notice was given (0 if none)
      `it materially prejudices me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are materially prejudiced by the variation (you must prove it)
      `settlement has happened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract has already settled
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I avoid for a notifiable variation` IF
        `under s 134`
    OR  ((NOT `settlement has happened`) AND `under s 135 or s 136`)
    WHERE
        `within 15 working days of any notice` MEANS
            (NOT `the seller has given notice of it at all`) OR `working days since the notice` AT MOST 15
        `under s 134` MEANS
                `the seller has given notice of it at all`
            AND `working days since the notice` AT MOST 15
            AND (NOT `the contract foretold it and it matched`)
            AND `it materially prejudices me`
            AND (NOT (`the variation` EQUALS `no notifiable variation`))
        `under s 135 or s 136` MEANS
            (NOT `the seller notified it in time`) AND `within 15 working days of any notice` AND
            CONSIDER `the variation`
            WHEN `a type 1 notifiable variation` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a type 2 notifiable variation` THEN `it materially prejudices me`
            OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 137(2): a contract for a lot not yet created "must -- (a) require any deposit or other amount payable by the buyer prior
-- to registration ... to be paid ... to a legal practitioner, real estate agent or settlement agent to be held on trust for
-- the buyer until the scheme is registered; and (b) specify the practitioner or agent". (3): the buyer may, "at any time
-- before registration ..., avoid" the contract if "(a) the contract does not comply with subsection (2); or (b) the lot is
-- not created -- (i) within a period after the date of the contract agreed in writing ...; or (ii) in the absence of such an
-- agreement, within 6 months after that date". The encoder counts whole months from the date of the contract (the later
-- signing day, s 137(4)).
@export As a buyer off the plan, may I avoid my contract because the deposit is not held on trust or my lot is not created in time (s 137)?
GIVEN `the lot has been created` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the scheme (or the amendment creating your lot) has been registered, creating the lot
      `the contract has the deposit held on trust by a named practitioner or agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract requires the deposit to be held on trust for you by a lawyer, real estate agent or settlement agent it names
      `a period was agreed in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the seller agreed in writing on a period for the lot to be created
      `the agreed period in months` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, that period in months; otherwise 0
      `whole months since the date of the contract` IS A NUMBER @desc Whole months since the contract was signed (by the last party to sign)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I avoid my off-the-plan contract` IF
        (NOT `the lot has been created`)
    AND (    (NOT `the contract has the deposit held on trust by a named practitioner or agent`)
          OR `whole months since the date of the contract` AT LEAST `the period`)
    WHERE
        `the period` MEANS
            IF `a period was agreed in writing` THEN `the agreed period in months` ELSE 6

-- s 138(2): on avoidance "(a) the buyer may recover from the seller as a debt all money paid by the buyer under the contract;
-- and (b) a person who is holding a deposit or other amount on behalf of the buyer ... must repay the deposit ... minus any
-- amount due to the seller as rent for any period during which the buyer was in occupation". The encoder reads the rent as
-- coming off the held deposit, and the rest of the money paid as owed by the seller.
@export If I avoid my contract to buy a lot, how much do I get back (s 138(2))?
GIVEN `the deposit held for me` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars held on your behalf as a deposit by an agent or practitioner
      `other money I paid the seller` IS A NUMBER @desc Any other dollars you paid the seller under the contract
      `rent due for my occupation` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars due to the seller as rent for any time you occupied the lot (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much do I get back` IS
    `the deposit held for me` MINUS `rent due for my occupation` PLUS `other money I paid the seller`

§§ `ss 162, 175 -- challenging a decision`

-- s 162(1): scheme disputes include "(a) a dispute between scheme participants" (s 162(2)(c): "a member of a community
-- corporation") about the community development statement, the scheme documents "including the validity of scheme
-- bylaws", "the performance of, or the failure to perform, a function", "an alleged contravention of this Act (other than an
-- offence)", "a resolution or decision of a community corporation or the council", "the appointment or election of a member
-- of the council or an officer"; "(f) a dispute between an applicant under section 94 and the community corporation" about
-- information, inspection and certificates; "(h) a dispute between a buyer or prospective buyer ... and the seller ... about
-- a matter arising under Part 10". (3): NOT scheme disputes -- "(a) a dispute with the Planning Commission ...; (b) a dispute
-- with the Registrar of Titles; (c) a dispute with the Valuer-General or a rating or taxing authority; (d) a dispute about a
-- contract of mortgage insurance under section 73; (e) a contractual dispute ... between (i) a scheme participant and a
-- person who is not a scheme participant ...; (f) a dispute about an amount owed as a debt". Unlike the Strata Titles Act
-- 1985 s 197(3)(f), (3)(f) here has no exception.
DECLARE `My dispute` IS ONE OF
    `the validity of a by-law`
    `a resolution or decision of the community corporation or its council`
    `the community corporation's failure to perform a function`
    `another owner's contravention of the Act`
    `the election of a council member or officer`
    `my application for information or a certificate`
    `the seller's disclosure when I bought the lot`
    `how much I owe the community corporation as a debt`
    `a contract with a contractor who is not a scheme participant`
    `rates or values set by the Valuer-General or a rating authority`
    `a decision of the Registrar of Titles`
    `my mortgage insurance contract`

@export Can I, as a lot owner, apply to the State Administrative Tribunal to resolve this dispute as a scheme dispute (s 162)?
GIVEN `the dispute` IS A `My dispute` @desc What the dispute is about
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I take this dispute to the Tribunal` IF
    CONSIDER `the dispute`
    WHEN `how much I owe the community corporation as a debt` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a contract with a contractor who is not a scheme participant` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `rates or values set by the Valuer-General or a rating authority` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a decision of the Registrar of Titles` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `my mortgage insurance contract` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 175(1): where the Tribunal "is constituted without a judicial member and ... makes an order or declaration of a kind
-- specified in the regulations, a party ... may apply for internal review". reg 173: "an order made by the Tribunal
-- constituted by a member who is not a legally qualified member is specified". (2): only "(a) [if] leave is given by the
-- Tribunal ... and (b) the application is made within 28 days after the order or declaration is made or within an extension
-- of that period given by the President". A member who is not legally qualified is taken to be not a judicial member
-- (inference). reg 173 names orders only, not declarations.
@export Can I apply for internal review of a Tribunal order made in my community titles dispute (s 175; reg 173)?
GIVEN `the order was made by a member who is not legally qualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal member who made the order is not a legally qualified member
      `the Tribunal gives leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal gives leave for the internal review
      `days since the order` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since the order was made
      `the President extended the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the President has extended the 28-day period (and you are within it)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I seek internal review` IF
        `the order was made by a member who is not legally qualified`
    AND `the Tribunal gives leave`
    AND (`days since the order` AT MOST 28 OR `the President extended the time`)
